{
 "cards": [
  {
   "dot": "cyan",
   "items": [
    "Only the joining node's ranges stream over the wire: ~9% of keys for 10 to 11, never a full rehash",
    "Bulk copy first, then catch up on writes until lag is near zero, and only then flip ownership",
    "In-flight requests during the flip are forwarded or safely retried — no stranded writes"
   ],
   "title": "Minimal remap on join"
  },
  {
   "dot": "emerald",
   "items": [
    "A 2x node takes 2x virtual nodes (ring) or 2x logical shards (fixed count): shares follow capacity",
    "Weights change only the new node's portion; every other key stays exactly where it was",
    "Virtual nodes also smooth the ring: 100 per node keeps the worst load near 1.2x the mean"
   ],
   "title": "Weights without rehash"
  },
  {
   "dot": "rose",
   "items": [
    "Data movement and routing updates are separate events: the map version flips after the data arrives",
    "Clients cache the map with a short TTL; a stale cache reads from the old owner, which forwards",
    "A leave mirrors a join: only the departed node's ranges are rehomed, replicas promote locally"
   ],
   "title": "Movement versus routing"
  }
 ],
